<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_trinket_10.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Enhancement Shaman Trinkets in Phase 1</span></h2>For trinkets, Enhancement Shamans aim for Agility, Mastery, Haste, or Critical Strike. Generally, two passive trinkets are preferred, but some fights might favor the damage profile of an on-use trinket.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87057/bottle-of-infinite-stars">
<img alt="Bottle of Infinite Stars" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bottle of Infinite Stars</span></a> is providing a lot of Mastery and a strong Agility proc on a short cooldown. It is a straight upgrade compared to the Zen Alchemist Stone, which is the Pre-Raid BiS.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87167/terror-in-the-mists">
<img alt="Terror in the Mists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Terror in the Mists</span></a> is offering a lot of Agility thanks to its item level. The Critical Strike proc is not the most desirable, but it is the only other high item level Agility available in this Tier.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
