<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as the  <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. This effectively means your abilities will never miss, though your regular swings still might.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them. For the vast majority of Raid bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry from behind. Expertise will also add to your Spell Hit. By reaching 7.5% in both Expertise and Hit, you will be able to reach 15% Spell Hit.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>You will try your best to match the sockets gem color whenever possible. The main goal is to stack Agility through your gems, but the extra Hit or Expertise allows for more optimal gearing and reforging. Avoid gemming pure Hit or Expertise, except for Engineering gems. However, if your gear won't allow you to reach your caps, try to gem the rest of the way, trying to match socket colors.<ul class="exclude-units">
